# SIFT-Bench clean-VM dry-run — 2026-06-08/09
# Host: docker python:3.12-slim (Debian trixie, arm64) on macOS laptop.
# Canonical target is x86-64 SIFT/Ubuntu 24.04; this is a from-scratch portability + reproducibility check.
# Proves the three no-image review paths from README "Reviewing without the memory image":
#   1. pip install -r requirements.txt resolves on a bare machine
#   2. scorer reproduces committed numbers from the judge cache with NO API key
#   3. unit tests pass (94)
# Fresh container has no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and .env is gitignored (never cloned), so all scoring below is cache-served.
# Large dpkg/pip progress and the two verbatim RAW JSON dumps are elided (marked); JSON is byte-identical to the committed score files noted inline.

